<addressbook><name>KOTO MASAHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OKAGAWA HIROAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OUCHI YOICHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SHIMIZU SUMITO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TADATOMO KAZUYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HAMAMURA, YUTAKA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HIRAMATSU, KAZUMASA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOTO, MASAHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OKAGAWA, HIROAKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OUCHI, YOICHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHIMIZU, SUMITO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TADATOMO, KAZUYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A semiconductor photodetector comprising a photodetecting layer (1) made of a GaN semiconductor and an electrode (2) so provided light (L) can be incident on a light-detecting surface (1a) which is one side of the photodetecting layer (1). If the photodetector is of Schottky barrier type, the electrode (2) includes a Schottky electrode so provided that the total length of the boundary line between the portion covered with the Schottky electrode of the photodetecting surface (1a) and the portion exposed is longer than the outer periphery of the photodetecting surface (1a). If the photodetector is of photoconductive type, the photodetecting layer (1) is an i layer of first conductivity type, the electrode (2) is an ohmic electrode of one polarity, and an ohmic electrode of the other polarity is provided on the other side of the photodetecting layer (1) directly or through a low-resistance GaN semiconductor layer of first conductivity type.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention porte sur un photodétecteur à semi-conducteur comportant une couche photodétectrice (1) de GaN ainsi qu'une électrode (2), la lumière (L) frappant sur une surface photodétectrice (1a) formant l'un des côtés de la couche photodétectrice (1). Si le photodétecteur est de type Schottky à barrière, l'électrode (2) comporte une électrode de Schottky telle que la longueur totale de la frontière séparant la partie recouverte de l'électrode de Schottky de la surface photodétectrice (1a) de la partie exposée soit supérieure à la périphérie extérieure de la surface photodétectrice (1a). Si le photodétecteur est du type à photoconduction, la couche photodétectrice (1) est une couche (i) d'un premier type de conductivité, l'électrode (2) est une électrode ohmique d'une polarité donnée, tandis que l'électrode ohmique de polarité inverse est formée par le deuxième côté de la couche photodétectrice, soit directement, soit par l'intermédiaire d'une couche de GaN de faible résistance, du premier type de conductivité.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>